;; A policy whose group names a SUBJECT GROUP the policy does not declare.
;;
;; It is a typo, and the emitted table is exactly where a typo would hide: the
;; table is total over the DECLARED set, so an undeclared name contributes no
;; row at all — and a group with no row for a subject group reads identically
;; to a group that deliberately does not receive it. There is nothing in the
;; emitted bytes for a consumer to notice.
;;
;; So `protocol-gen.projection` refuses it by name instead, and it does so at
;; POLICY grain rather than group grain because the declared set is a top-level
;; declaration no single group can see.
{:version 1
 :subject-groups ["diagnostics" "telemetry"]
 :groups
 [{:id :sensor-reader
   :package "pgfix.sensor"
   :grants [{:message "pgfix.Reading" :access #{:read} :fields #{"value"}}]
   :subject-groups ["telemetry" "thermla"]}]}
